</section>
<section id="Ax1.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.2 </span>Ablation on Number of Training Epochs</h4>

<div id="Ax1.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We investigate the effects of training duration by training for 1, 3, 5, 7, and 10 epochs. Results are reported in <a href="#Ax1.T8" title="In C.2 Ablation on Number of Training Epochs ‣ C Additional Ablations ‣ Appendices ‣ CLIP Is Shortsighted: Paying Attention Beyond the First Sentence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. We observe that performance improves substantially across datasets when increasing from 1 to 3 epochs (<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+2.9\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2.9</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+2.9\%</annotation></semantics></math> on Urban1k T2I), with more marginal but consistent gains from 3 to 5 and 5 to 7 epochs. Improvements for long retrieval from 7 to 10 epochs are minor (<math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2\%</annotation></semantics></math>), and short retrieval is starting to be negatively affected. We also include the original Long-CLIP results for comparison. Notably, even with an equivalent training budget (1 epoch), our DeBias-CLIP method significantly outperforms the Long-CLIP baseline for all datasets, with <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1.8\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1.8</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1.8\%</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+2.3\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2.3</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+2.3\%</annotation></semantics></math> for short-text retrieval on COCO and Flickr T2I, and <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+10.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>10.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+10.6\%</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+7.0\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>7.0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+7.0\%</annotation></semantics></math> for long-text retrieval on Urban1k and DOCCI T2I.</p>
</div>
